{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, good idea to do this before your password expires! Your account is in good shape and you're set up with Duo on your phone, so you can change the password yourself. Two ways to do it: (1) On your laptop, connect to the office network or VPN first. Press Ctrl+Alt+Delete, choose 'Change a password', enter your current password, then type your new one twice. (2) Or use the self-service password reset link on the company sign-in page and approve the Duo push on your phone when it asks. Your new password needs at least 14 characters and can't be one you've used recently. After you change it, sign in again with the new password on your phone and any other devices that get email. One more thing: your mailbox is about 99% full. Once it's completely full, you may stop getting new email, so it's worth deleting or archiving old messages soon. Let us know if anything doesn't work.",
  "internal_note": "P4 how-to. Sender verified (request came from her own email). lookup_user: user_id 9, account active, 0 failed logins, must_change_password false, not blocked, not VIP. check_mfa_status: enrolled in Duo (duo_push, Mei's phone), so she qualifies for self-service reset under KB-002 Fix step 1. Gave her the self-service steps plus the Ctrl+Alt+Del change option on the laptop while on the office network or VPN (KB-003). Reminded her of the policy: 14+ characters, no reuse. No admin reset needed, nothing queued. Also noticed: mailbox is at 99.4% (50890/51200 MB). I warned the user. May need a follow-up if she asks for more space.",
